un too get your hands  dirty  okay so I've got my butter all spread on  there don't worry about how it looks now  it doesn't look so pretty now but when  it comes out of the oven it's going to  look pretty so take the wings and just  kind of fold them the wing tips around  the back of the bird like that it's  ready to go on my roasting rack I'll  take my gloves off and the most  important thing to do now is to put our  thermometer in there I'd say it takes  about two and a half three and a half  hours but more importantly is  temperature so put the thermometer in  the thickest part of the breast set it  to 160. and then in the oven it's going  to go  until it's done  [Music]  okay we'll let the turkey do its thing  okay guys my turkey came out of the oven  looking awesome  um the butter and all the herbs just  kind of just just melt away and the skin  gets crispy golden brown and looks  fantastic just be sure that you cook it  to the right temperature use that meat  thermometer make sure you get to the  right temperature I say 160 to pull it  because that's like as it rests the  temperature goes up but make sure that  your interior of the thickest part of  the breast gets to 165 that's what  you're mainly worried about but either  way it's fantastic this great this  turkey is missing gravy though right  actually if you look in that if you  download or get yourself a copy of the  of the coloring book cookbook on the  website or again in store it has a  recipe to go ahead and make a gravy on  that same one so I urge you to do that  because your turkey needs gravy right I  wish you guys all the best of  Thanksgiving and all of your holidays  remember it doesn't matter what you make  as long as you're making memories right  thank you so much for watching thank you  for shopping and we will see you all  next time bye everyone  visit smithsmoodanddrug.com for more  information JC
 

